.TH "ipp-usb-api" "7" "2026-10-31" "Control API for ipp-usb"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
ipp-usb-api - Control API for \fBipp-usb\fR daemon
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBipp-usb\fR control API provides a way for local client
applications to communicate with the running \fBipp-usb\fR daemon.\&
.PP
The API uses a UNIX domain socket.\&
.PP
.SH PROTOCOL
.PP
.SS Overview
.PP
The control API uses HTTP over a UNIX domain socket.\& Requests are
sent using the HTTP GET and POST methods.\&
.PP
The protocol is versioned independently of the \fBipp-usb\fR software
release.\& The protocol version identifies the \fBipp-usb\fR release in
which the latest protocol changes were introduced.\& It remains
unchanged across software releases that do not change the protocol.\&
.PP
The protocol is backward compatible.\& New endpoints and request
parameters may be introduced in later protocol versions without
breaking existing clients.\&
.PP
The protocol version in which each endpoint and each request or
response field was introduced is documented below.\&
.PP
.SS Authentication
.PP
Information requests are available to everyone.\& Administrative
requests require authentication.\&
.PP
Since all communication takes place over an \fB\fRAF_UNIX\fB\fR socket,
the server uses the \fB\fRSO_PEERCRED\fB\fR socket option to obtain the
UID of the calling user.\&
.PP
To authorize administrative requests, the calling user must be
granted \fB\fRadmin\fB\fR permission in the \fB\fRipp-usb.\&conf\fB\fR file.\&
.PP
See the \fB\fRAuthentication\fB\fR section in \fBipp-usb(8)\fR for details
on configuring authentication.\&
.PP
.SH REQUESTS
.PP
.SS GET /status (since 0.9.22)
.PP
\fBAuthentication required\fR: none
.br
\fBResponse Content-Type:\fR text/plain
.PP
This is a legacy request.\& It returns a formatted status page
containing the same information as the output of the ipp-usb status
command.\&
.PP
.SS GET /version (since 0.9.35)
.PP
\fBAuthentication required\fR: none
.br
\fBResponse Content-Type:\fR text/plain
.PP
Returns the protocol version as a plain-text string.\&
.PP
The version identifies the \fBipp-usb\fR release in which the latest
protocol changes were introduced.\& For example:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
0\&.9\&.35
.fi
.RE
.PP
The returned version does not necessarily match the version of the
running ipp-usb daemon.\&
.PP
Assume version \fB0.\&9.\&22\fR if \fB404 Not found\fR error is returned.\&
.PP
.SS POST /get/conf (since 0.9.35)
.PP
\fBAuthentication required\fR: none
.br
\fBRequest Content-Type:\fR application/json
.br
\fBResponse Content-Type:\fR application/json
.PP
\fBRequest data:\fR
.nf
.RS 4
    {
      // Device identification; all fields are optional
      "usb_MFG"  : "Xerox",
      "usb_MDL"  : "B235 MFP",
      "usb_SN"   : "34004H030206H",
      "usb_HWID" : "0924&9d3b",
      "usb_URI"  : "usb://Xerox/B235%20MFP?serial=34004H030206H",
    }
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBError response:\fR
.nf
.RS 4
    {
      "err": "error message"
    }
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBData response:\fR
.nf
.RS 4
    {
      // Array of devices, matching the search criteria
      "data": [
        {
          // Device identification
          "usb_MFG"  : "Xerox",
          "usb_MDL"  : "B235 MFP",
          "usb_SN"   : "34004H030206H",
          "usb_HWID" : "0924&9d3b",
          "usb_URI"  : "usb://Xerox/B235%20MFP?serial=34004H030206H",

          // Settings
          "disabled" : true | false,
        },
      ]
    }
.fi
.RE
.PP
This request returns array of per-device configuration records.\&
Parameters of request specify search criteria.\& If no matching
devices were found, empty array is returned.\&
.PP
.SS POST /set/conf (since 0.9.35)
.PP
\fBAuthentication required\fR: admin
.br
\fBRequest Content-Type:\fR application/json
.br
\fBResponse Content-Type:\fR application/json
.PP
\fBRequest data:\fR
.nf
.RS 4
    {
      // Device identification; all fields are optional
      "usb_MFG"  : "Xerox",
      "usb_MDL"  : "B235 MFP",
      "usb_SN"   : "34004H030206H",
      "usb_HWID" : "0924&9d3b",
      "usb_URI"  : "usb://Xerox/B235%20MFP?serial=34004H030206H",

      // Settings -- supply only parameters that
      // should be changed\&.
      "disabled" : true | false,
    }
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBError response:\fR
.nf
.RS 4
    {
      "err": "error message"
    }
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBData response:\fR
.nf
.RS 4
    {
      // Empty
      "data": {
        // Device identification
        "usb_MFG"  : "Xerox",
        "usb_MDL"  : "B235 MFP",
        "usb_SN"   : "34004H030206H",
        "usb_HWID" : "0924&9d3b",
        "usb_URI"  : "usb://Xerox/B235%20MFP?serial=34004H030206H",

        // Settings
        "disabled" : true | false,
      },
    }
.fi
.RE
.PP
Device identification in the request should be unambigous,
which means that at least any combibation of the identification
parameters is provided:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
usb_MFG + usb_MDL + usb_SN
.IP \(bu 4
usb_HWID + usb_SN
.IP \(bu 4
usb_URI
.PD
.PP
Note, this definition of unambigous identification doesn'\&t
depend on amount of known devices and only depend on
request parameters.\&
.PP
Only those setting parameters that intendent to be changed
should be provided in the request.\& Multiple parameters
can be changed by a single request.\&
.PP
Upon succesful completion, settings are persisted on disk
and the state of already connected devices are updated
appropriately.\&
.PP
This request returns an updated device configuration record.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB/var/ipp-usb/ctrl\fR
.RS 4
\fBipp-usb\fR control socket
.PP
.RE
